    "guidance": "Preferred default when extraction/lift/transfer phase ambiguity or premature below-roof transfer is the main concern: it passed 12/12 in-distribution runs, ended with drawer_position about 0.300 throughout, and had zero IK-unconverged steps. Use only with training-like world/tunnel geometry, an open stable drawer, a valid target_pose, and a low tunnel block; its narrow guard conservatively caps destination-directed +x motion when closed-near-object proxies indicate the block is below 0.16 m. Avoid if target_pose/geometry is unreliable, if a valid unseen maneuver intentionally requires low transfer, or if failed-grasp recovery is needed; use h01 only for the unvalidated displaced-block specialization and h02 for a major valid TCP/configuration mismatch. Failure signs are closed fingers without object/TCP coupling, repeated guard intervention while the block stays low, failure to rise, drop, destination drift, drawer_position <=0.26, or persistent IK nonconvergence/limits. Hand off in 680:840 once coupling persists, the block is outside with its bottom above the roof (or already inside), drawer_position >0.26, the guard is inactive, and transfer is directed toward the drawer."
